<title>USA: Amphenol sets special meeting for May 14.</title>
<headline>Amphenol sets special meeting for May 14.</headline>
<dateline>WALLINGFORD, Conn. 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amphenol Corp said Wednesday that it would hold a special meeting of shareholders on May 14, 1997 to vote on the proposed merger agreement of Amphenol and NXS Acquisition Corp, an affiliate of Kohlberg Kravis Roberts &amp; Co.</p>
<p>As previously announced in January, the deal which is valued at $1.5 billion including refinanced debt will provide NXS Acquisition with over 75 percent of Amphenol.</p>
<p>Up to 10 percent of Amphenol stock, or 4.4 million share can be retained by shareholders. The terms are $26 cash per share.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
